Tax Code Identification System - Technical Documentation
Use Case: AI-Powered Tax Code Recommendation for Invoice Line Items Based on Historical Data

1. Executive Summary
1.1 Business Problem
In enterprise finance and accounts payable operations, organizations frequently encounter challenges when determining the correct tax code for invoice line items. This challenge is particularly significant when:

Multiple valid tax codes exist for similar product/service descriptions
Tax regulations vary by country, vendor, and product category
Manual tax code assignment is time-consuming and error-prone
Consistency across similar transactions is hard to maintain
Historical patterns and precedents need to be leveraged for accuracy
Organizations need an automated solution that learns from historical transactions and provides intelligent recommendations.

1.2 Solution Overview
The Tax Code Identification System automatically recommends tax codes for invoice line items using historical data analysis, vector similarity search, and LLM-based reasoning.

Technique	Purpose
Vector Similarity Search	Finds semantically similar historical transactions using Azure AI Search
Historical Pattern Analysis	Analyzes past tax code assignments for similar line items
LLM Reasoning (Azure OpenAI)	Generates context-aware tax code recommendations with justifications
Confidence Scoring	Calculates a confidence score based on multiple weighted factors
1.3 Key Capabilities
Semantic Matching: Uses embeddings to find similar historical line item descriptions
Multi-Factor Filtering: Filters by company code, country, vendor, and tax percentage
AI-Powered Recommendations: Uses Azure OpenAI to analyze and recommend the best tax code
Confidence Scoring: Provides a weighted confidence score based on similarity, frequency, recency, and parameter matching
Parallel Processing: Processes multiple invoice line items concurrently using ThreadPoolExecutor
Automatic Data Ingestion: Auto-uploads new historical data from CSV files to Azure AI Search
Dynamic Configuration: All field mappings and parameters are configurable via config file
